Z||000000||rnoswal||01-15-2001||02:55 PM||||I own an 85 with the 4 cyl engine. I saw an 86 SE, V-6 at the junkyard today. The v-6 has an automatic, but I want to keep my 5 speed. Will it bolt in and how about electronics. I know I need the V-6 fuel pump. Do I need to find a v-6 flywheel or does the 4 cyl flywheel bolt on? It is a 2.8.<P>Thanks<BR>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||01-15-2001||03:02 PM||||flywheels are interchangable... at least on an (87-4 to 86-V6, Black GT (todd)) is running that) you'll need an ECU, wiring harness, fuel pump, Intake system or decent mounting for MAT sensor, probly rear springs too... it should be pretty straight forward... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rnoswal||01-15-2001||07:48 PM||||Thanks. Now, will any of the wiring plug into the existing wiring or do I need an electronics expert to figure this out?<P>Thanks again    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by rnoswal (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-15-2001||08:24 PM||||Just get the wiring harness form the v6 donor car and swap it with the engine. It’s easy with the fiero. I took my whole wiring harness out with my motor in not time.<P>You need the v6 wiring harness.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dman||01-15-2001||09:12 PM||||Hello everyone. The only thing I'd like to add to is to suggest you use a V6 flywheel from an 85, 86 or 87, I don't believe the L4 has the same balancing characteristics. The 86 V6 is externally balanced by the flywheel, if you use the 85 L4 flywheel I'm not sure it will balance properly. If it doesn't you'll get lots of vibration.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ray b||01-15-2001||10:27 PM|||| don't forget raideater v6 is 2 row 4 is one.||||reg||1
